# Superpowers scratch output is ignored by default, but plans are deliverables and
# belong in version control. Without the re-includes below, `git add docs/` silently
# skips this whole subtree — plan files then track only via `git add -f`, which is a
# habit that eventually loses one.
#
# `!plans/` must come before `!plans/**`: git will not re-include a file inside an
# excluded directory unless the directory itself is re-included first.
*
!.gitignore
!plans/
!plans/**
